Enhancement: Store stable device IDs for hardlinked files

Restic stores the device ID of hardlinked files to recreate the hardlinks when
restoring a snapshot. Filesystems like btrfs and ZFS report a new device ID
whenever a subvolume or a filesystem snapshot is mounted. This changed the
metadata of every hardlinked file and made restic upload a new copy of the
whole directory metadata on every backup run.

Restic now stores a virtual device ID that stays the same across backup runs.

This is part of the alpha feature `device-id-for-hardlinks`. That feature now
stores a device ID only for nodes that can be hardlinked. Enable it by setting
the environment variable `RESTIC_FEATURES=device-id-for-hardlinks`.

The first backup after enabling the feature rewrites the metadata of all
directories once and therefore uploads more data than usual. Later backup runs
are unaffected.

